OpenRouter Spend for KDE Plasma 5 (KF5 / Qt 5.15). Same figures as the Omarchy bar widget: a panel pill, and a breakdown popup when you click it.

This branch (`plasma5-qt5-port`) targets Plasma 5.27 / KF5 / Qt 5.15. The `master` version of this package targets Plasma 6 (root `PlasmoidItem`, versionless KF6 imports) and will not load on Plasma 5: on a KF5 shell the applet is never even instantiated, so nothing is drawn. The two QML APIs are not source compatible, so the package is single-target.

KDE widget docs (check these when changing QML or metadata): https://develop.kde.org/docs/plasma/widget/

Panel: wallet icon plus a pill with `$<month> ($<24h>, $<1h>)`. Click for the full breakdown popup.

Popup: month total, last 30 days stacked by model, last hour in 5-minute buckets, spend per model, spend per day. Days cut off at local midnight.

Management key: widget settings only (`sk-or-...` placeholder in docs — never commit real keys). Cache: `Qt.labs.settings`, group `OpenRouterSpend` (QtQuick.LocalStorage is a separately packaged module on KF5 distros, so it is not used here).

What differs from the Plasma 6 version:

- applet root is a plain `Item`; representations hang off `Plasmoid.compactRepresentation` / `Plasmoid.fullRepresentation`
- metadata.json carries the KF5 keys `X-Plasma-API: declarativeappletscript` and `X-Plasma-MainScript: ui/main.qml`, and does **not** set `X-Plasma-API-Minimum-Version: 6.0` (KF5 refuses to load an applet that demands a newer API)
- config page root is a bare `Kirigami.FormLayout`, not `KCM.SimpleKCM`
- `Plasmoid.action("configure").trigger()` opens the settings dialog (`internalAction` does not exist in KF5)
- not available in KF5 and therefore removed: `PlasmoidItem`, `badgeText`, `Plasmoid.secondaryActivated()`, `Qt.alpha()`

Install from the repo root:

```
kpackagetool5 -t Plasma/Applet -i cachyos-kde-widget
```

Add **OpenRouter Spend** to a panel. Right-click the pill → Configure, and paste an OpenRouter management key (`sk-or-...`). The gear in the popup opens the same dialog.

After later changes:

```
kpackagetool5 -t Plasma/Applet -u cachyos-kde-widget
```

If the widget does not appear in the picker, restart the shell:

```
systemctl --user restart plasma-plasmashell.service
```
